<title>GERMANY: German grain trade seeks intervention rye export.</title>
<headline>German grain trade seeks intervention rye export.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders placed bids for the export of 121,951 tonnes of intervention rye to third countries at the weekly European Union export tender, state intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bids were made under a 209,667 tonne rye tender opened by the EU for Germany with effect from today.</p>
<p>No other bids for intervention grain were received.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
